# Default protected-path patterns for the merge-content gate (Lesson 1 from the
# AutoCraft deep study, adopted 2026-11-19). One glob per line; blank lines and
# lines whose first non-space character is # are ignored. Patterns are matched
# against changed paths with bash glob semantics, so `*/` matches any leading
# directory depth and a bare name matches at the repository root only when no
# nested variant is listed alongside it.
#
# A project may replace this list entirely with its own
# <project>/config/protected-paths; a present-but-empty file there disarms the
# gate and every merge is refused until the list is restored.
#
# Classes are the captain's adopted rulings: CI/workflow configuration,
# agent-instruction files, lockfiles, submodule pointers, and binaries. Mode
# changes on executable scripts are gated by review policy rather than here,
# because a name-based gate cannot see the executable bit.

# ---- CI / workflow configuration ----
.github/workflows/*
*/.github/workflows/*
.gitlab-ci.yml
*/.gitlab-ci.yml
Jenkinsfile
*/Jenkinsfile
azure-pipelines.yml
*/azure-pipelines.yml
.circleci/config.yml
*/.circleci/config.yml
.travis.yml
*/.travis.yml
.bitbucket-pipelines.yml
*/.bitbucket-pipelines.yml
.drone.yml
*/.drone.yml
azure-pipelines.yaml
*/azure-pipelines.yaml
cloudbuild.yaml
*/cloudbuild.yaml
.forgejo/workflows/*
*/.forgejo/workflows/*
.gitea/workflows/*
*/.gitea/workflows/*
.woodpecker/*
*/.woodpecker/*
.buildkite/*
*/.buildkite/*
.teamcity/*
*/.teamcity/*

# ---- Agent instruction files ----
AGENTS.md
*/AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
*/CLAUDE.md

